index 3b36685..55d5562 100644
--- a/docs/FORMAT.md
+++ b/docs/FORMAT.md
@@ -51,6 +51,30 @@ default commodity, which is displayed without a suffix. Each transaction must
 balance in every commodity separately. A posting may omit its amount only when
 all the other postings use the same commodity; it takes that commodity.
 
+## Costs
+
+A posting's amount may be followed by `@` and a cost, separated by
+whitespace on both sides. The cost is the price of one unit of the
+posting's commodity, in another commodity:
+
+```text
+2026-02-01 Buy shares
+    Assets:Broker      10 AAPL @ 150.00 USD
+    Assets:Checking
+```
+
+For balancing, a posting with a cost weighs its quantity times its cost
+(`-4 AAPL @ 175 USD` weighs -700 USD); every other posting weighs its
+amount. A transaction must balance in every commodity of the weights,
+and an elided amount receives the balancing weight. The cost must be a
+positive number in a commodity other than the quantity's.
+
+`print` and `forecast` write the cost after the amount
+(`10.00 AAPL @ 150.00 USD`). Reports show quantities, except that
+`balance --cost`, `register --cost` and `networth --cost` count each posting with a cost as its
+weight, before any `--convert`. Costs are not prices: `prices` and
+`--convert` use only `P` directives.
+
 ## Prices
 
 A price directive starts in column one:
